  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Sinhala names are a given name and a family name (Kasun Perera, Nadeesha Jayasinghe). Many family names are Portuguese in origin (Perera, Fernando, Silva) from the colonial era, others are old Sinhala lineage names (Bandara, Dissanayake, Wickramasinghe); formal names can carry a long ancestral house name (vasagama) first, often shortened to initials. Sri Lankan Tamils traditionally have no fixed family name: the father's given name is used as the surname or as an initial (Arun Sivakumar is Arun, son of Sivakumar). Sri Lankan Muslims (Moors) use Arabic origin names, often with the father's name or an old family name like Marikar or Lebbe. Christians among both Sinhala and Tamil communities carry names like Anthony, Joseph or Mary with their own.",
